    "<a href='https://gis.conservationhalton.net/doc/opendatahub/metadata/CH_Metatdata_FC_Halton_Hamilton_Rainfall_Grid_20140804.pdf' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Click Here</a><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'> for Metadata. This GIS layer is part of the dataset containing map layers related to the August 4th, 2014 rainfall storm event.  The dataset shows the United States National Weather Service Buffalo Weather Radar Doppler radar generated and total rain gauge adjusted rainfall estimates (mm) for the August 4th, 2014 storm in a 1km2 gridded format. The rainfall amounts derived from the radar station were adjusted using the rainfall totals in the rain gauge GIS layer.</span>"
